# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Agent Guide

This repository uses the AI Governance Starter Kit. Treat this file as the
primary agent entrypoint before planning, editing, validating, or committing.

## Working rules

- Preserve existing user work. Check `git status` before destructive commands,
  commits, or broad rewrites.
- Keep the project buildable. Run the relevant validation scripts before
  completing code changes.
- For risky, cross-cutting, security, data, billing, auth, migration, or
  production-adjacent work, create or activate a Micro-Spec before
  implementation.
- Use server-side or authoritative systems for state that affects users,
  money, permissions, compliance, or audit trails.
- Do not add generated planning packs, screenshots, or evidence folders unless
  the task or active Micro-Spec requires them.

## Governance files

- `AGENTS.md`: repository working rules and routing.
- `Instructions_MicroSpecsCreation.md`: how to author Micro-Specs.
- `Instructions_tdd.md`: implementation workflow when a Micro-Spec is active.
- `micro-specs/README.md`: governance index, lifecycle, risk classes, and gates.
- `micro-specs/GLOBAL_CONTEXT.md`: repo-specific constraints.
- `scripts/check-governance.mjs`: validates Micro-Spec metadata and blast radius.
- `scripts/run-governance-gates.mjs`: runs gates declared by active Micro-Specs.

